+"""Per-tick service-gain tracker -- feeds GMAX's marginal-goodput function.
+
+Architectural role (paper §4.2 b_min book-keeping and §6.3 "marginal
+goodput per SLO class"):
+
+    Service gain quantifies how much each scheduling tick contributes to
+    a request's eventual goodput, given its SLO class. The values
+    computed here become the per-request "reward" used by SLOPolicy in
+    scheduler/policy.py to derive the GMAX priority on the next tick.
+
+    For latency-sensitive requests (_latency_service_gain below):
+    contribution accumulates as the sum of a TTFT-bounded prefill term --
+    penalised by the ratio (TTFT_constraint / realised_TTFT) raised to
+    penalty_factor when the actual TTFT overruns the SLO -- and a decode
+    term, penalised by the ratio (output_len_so_far / desired_decode_len)
+    when the realised decode rate falls behind the per-token rate target
+    set by TBT_constraint. _desired_decode_len() implements that
+    per-token rate target directly: it converts the TBT_constraint and
+    elapsed time into the number of tokens the request *should* have
+    produced by now, which is the same rate target b_min in §4.2.
+
+    For deadline-sensitive and compound requests (_throughput_service_gain
+    below): contribution is weighted by min(1, deadline / TTLT) raised to
+    penalty_factor, so a request that has already overshot its deadline
+    contributes a vanishing service gain; a comfortable request
+    contributes its full prefill + decode tokens.
+
+    The "concord_metrics" attached to each SequenceGroup is the canonical
+    record of TTFT, TBT samples, and the running service_gain that
+    SLOPolicy queries through reward_estimation().
+"""
+
